{"repositoryId":397563881,"availability":"available","full":"carina-io/carina","name":"carina","description":"Carina: an high performance and ops-free local storage for kubernetes","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":727,"forks":85,"created":"2021-08-18T10:41:10Z","updated":"2025-04-16T07:49:27Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://carina-io.github.io","topics":["autotiering","csi","high-performance","kubernetes","latency","local","lvm","opsfree","raw","storage"],"demo":"https://carina-io.github.io/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.819Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.819Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.819Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.819Z","stars":727,"forks":85}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Storage systems are complex! There are more and more kubernetes native storage systems nowadays and stateful applications are shifting into cloud native world, for example, modern databases and middlewares. However, both modern databases and its storage providers try to solve some common problems in their own way. For example, they both deal with data replications and consistency. This introduces a giant waste of both capacity and performance and needs more mantainness effort. And besides that, stateful applications strive to be more peformant, eliminating every possible latency, which is…","Carina is a standard kubernetes CSI plugin. Users can use standard kubernetes storage resources like storageclass/PVC/PV to request storage media. The key considerations of carina includes:","In short, Carina strives to provide extremely-low-latency and noOps storage system for cloudnative databases and be DBA expert of the storage domain in cloudnative era!"],"features":["Workloads need different storage systems. Carina will focus on cloudnative database scenario usage only.","Completely kubernetes native and easy to install.","Using local disks and group them as needed, user can provison different type of disks using different storage class.","Scaning physical disks and building a RAID as required. If disk fails, just plugin a new one and it's done.","Node capacity and performance aware, so scheduling pods more smartly."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/carina-io/carina/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"430211c2bd61eeb75eb5f5e5dd36efe1915422565b4cbad0197b8d2eb8bc9f62","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.965Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.965Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Storage systems are complex! There are more and more kubernetes native storage systems nowadays and stateful applications are shifting into cloud native world, for example, modern databases and middlewares. However, both modern databases and its storage providers try to solve some common problems in their own way. For example, they both deal with data replications and consistency. This introduces a giant waste of both capacity and performance and needs more mantainness effort. And besides that, stateful applications strive to be more peformant, eliminating every possible latency, which is…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/carina-io/carina/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"430211c2bd61eeb75eb5f5e5dd36efe1915422565b4cbad0197b8d2eb8bc9f62","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/carina-io/carina/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.966Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-04-16T07:49:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/carina-io/carina/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:47.966Z","hash":"430211c2bd61eeb75eb5f5e5dd36efe1915422565b4cbad0197b8d2eb8bc9f62","originalBytes":8715,"storedBytes":8715,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["carina","docs","yes","manual","storage","disk","high","kubernetes","data","disks","standard","cloudnative","pods","support","different","node","performance","specific","capac